    "turn": {
      "duration": 2.2,
      "loop": false,
      "note": "A 12 deg yaw, held, and released. Every number in it is one line of arithmetic on dx = x (cos t - 1) - z sin t, the projection of a yaw about the skull's axis: the two mesh deforms carry the face and fringe plates, `faceshift` carries the shift every feature shares, and each feature's own translatex carries only its parallax — its depth relative to the skull, times sin t. The anticipation lives in `headroll`'s roll and not in the yaw, because a yaw anticipation costs a whole 50-number deform key. The iris and its highlight carry the RECIPROCAL of their socket's scaleX: the socket foreshortens, the eyeball counter-rotates to keep looking at the viewer, and a pupil that goes elliptical is what stops a turn reading at 18 deg instead of 26. README.md derives all of it and measures where it stops reading.",

      "tracks": [
        {
          "bone": "faceshift",
          "property": "translatex",
          "keys": [
            { "t": 0, "v": [0], "ease": "rise" },
            { "t": 0.62, "v": [-35.345], "ease": "swell" },
